### Day 22 Lab — RFC 7523 Client Authentication HTTP Examples

## Part 1: DCR Registration with `private_key_jwt`

### Request: Register Payment Orchestrator Client

POST https://<PLACEHOLDER: is-host>:9443/api/identity/oauth2/dcr/v1.1/register
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic <PLACEHOLDER: admin-credentials-base64>

{
  "client_name": "payment-orchestrator",
  "client_uri": "https://<PLACEHOLDER: fintech-host>",
  "grant_types": [
    "authorization_code",
    "urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange"
  ],
  "redirect_uris": [
    "https://<PLACEHOLDER: fintech-host>/oauth/callback"
  ],
  "response_types": [
    "code"
  ],
  "token_endpoint_auth_method": "private_key_jwt",
  "jwks_uri": "https://<PLACEHOLDER: fintech-host>/.well-known/jwks.json",
  "require_auth_time": false
}

### Response: DCR Registration Success

HTTP/1.1 201 Created
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "client_id": "payment-orchestrator-v1",
  "client_secret": null,
  "client_id_issued_at": <PLACEHOLDER: unix-timestamp>,
  "client_name": "payment-orchestrator",
  "grant_types": [
    "authorization_code",
    "urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange"
  ],
  "redirect_uris": [
    "https://<PLACEHOLDER: fintech-host>/oauth/callback"
  ],
  "response_types": [
    "code"
  ],
  "token_endpoint_auth_method": "private_key_jwt",
  "jwks_uri": "https://<PLACEHOLDER: fintech-host>/.well-known/jwks.json"
}

---

## Part 2: Token Request with `client_assertion` (Form Body)

### Request: Token Exchange with JWT Bearer Assertion

POST https://<PLACEHOLDER: is-host>:9443/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code
&code=<PLACEHOLDER: authorization-code>
&redirect_uri=https://<PLACEHOLDER: fintech-host>/oauth/callback
&client_assertion_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:client-assertion-type:jwt-bearer
&client_assertion=<PLACEHOLDER: base64url-encoded-jwt>

### Client Assertion JWT Payload (Decoded)

Before encoding, the JWT contains:

{
  "alg": "RS256",
  "kid": "2024-fintech-key-001",
  "typ": "JWT"
}

---HEADER ABOVE, PAYLOAD BELOW---

{
  "iss": "payment-orchestrator-v1",
  "sub": "payment-orchestrator-v1",
  "aud": "https://<PLACEHOLDER: is-host>:9443/oauth2/token",
  "jti": "<PLACEHOLDER: UUIDv4>",
  "exp": <PLACEHOLDER: unix-timestamp now+300>,
  "iat": <PLACEHOLDER: unix-timestamp now>
}

### Breakdown of JWT Claims

| Claim | Value | Purpose |
|-------|-------|---------|
| `iss` | `payment-orchestrator-v1` | **Issuer** — who signed this JWT? Must match client_id. |
| `sub` | `payment-orchestrator-v1` | **Subject** — who is the subject of this assertion? For client auth, same as `iss`. |
| `aud` | `https://<host>:9443/oauth2/token` | **Audience** — who should accept this JWT? Must match token endpoint URL exactly. Prevents reuse at other endpoints. |
| `jti` | `<UUIDv4>` | **JWT ID** — unique identifier. IS 7.3 caches this to prevent replay. Generate fresh UUID per request. |
| `exp` | `now+300` | **Expiration** — when does this assertion expire? Max 5 min recommended. IS 7.3 may reject if > 5 min. |
| `iat` | `now` | **Issued At** — when was this JWT issued? Sanity check for clock skew. |

### Response: Token Issued

HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "access_token": "<PLACEHOLDER: issued-jwt>",
  "token_type": "Bearer",
  "expires_in": 3600,
  "scope": "authorization_code"
}

### Issued Access Token Payload (Decoded)

{
  "sub": "payment-orchestrator-v1",
  "aud": [
    "https://<PLACEHOLDER: resource-server-1>",
    "https://<PLACEHOLDER: resource-server-2>"
  ],
  "iss": "https://<PLACEHOLDER: is-host>:9443/oauth2/token",
  "azp": "payment-orchestrator-v1",
  "scope": "authorization_code",
  "auth_time": <PLACEHOLDER: unix-timestamp>,
  "exp": <PLACEHOLDER: unix-timestamp now+3600>,
  "iat": <PLACEHOLDER: unix-timestamp now>,
  "jti": "<PLACEHOLDER: new-UUIDv4>"
}

---

## Part 3: CRITICAL — What NOT to Do

### ❌ WRONG: Authorization Header with Bearer

```
POST /oauth2/token
Authorization: Bearer <PLACEHOLDER: client-assertion>
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code
&code=<auth-code>
&redirect_uri=https://fintech.local/callback
```

**Why this fails:**
- IS 7.3 interprets `Authorization: Bearer` as a resource access token, not client authentication
- The `client_assertion` in the header is ignored
- IS 7.3 sees: anonymous request, no client_id, no authentication
- Result: `401 Unauthorized` or `invalid_client`

**Correct approach:**
- Put `client_assertion` in the **form body** (POST body, not header)
- Include `client_assertion_type` also in form body
- No `Authorization` header needed (IS 7.3 extracts client_id from JWT `iss` claim)

---

## Part 4: Subsequent Token Exchange (RFC 8693)

After receiving the access token above, the client can use it for token exchange:

### Request: Token Exchange for Agent Delegation

POST https://<PLACEHOLDER: is-host>:9443/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange
&subject_token=<PLACEHOLDER: user-access-token>
&subject_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:access_token
&actor_token=<PLACEHOLDER: orchestrator-jwt-assertion>
&actor_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt
&scope=payments:initiate
&requested_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:access_token
&client_assertion_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:client-assertion-type:jwt-bearer
&client_assertion=<PLACEHOLDER: new-jwt-for-this-request>

### Note

For token exchange, the client AGAIN authenticates with `private_key_jwt`:
- Generate a **new** JWT assertion (fresh `jti`, fresh `iat`/`exp`)
- Include it in the token exchange request as `client_assertion`
- IS 7.3 validates this assertion before processing the exchange

---

## Troubleshooting: Common Errors

### Error: `invalid_client: JWKS validation failed`

**Possible causes:**
1. JWKS URI unreachable from IS 7.3's network (firewall, DNS, SSL/TLS issue)
   - **Fix:** Check network connectivity. Verify JWKS URI in DCR is correct. Test: `curl https://fintech.local/.well-known/jwks.json`
2. JWT algorithm mismatch (JWT uses RS256, JWKS has only ES256)
   - **Fix:** Ensure JWT `alg` matches a key in JWKS with same algorithm
3. JWT `kid` not in JWKS (key rotation mismatch)
   - **Fix:** Ensure the `kid` in JWT header matches a `kid` in JWKS. Implement key rotation with overlap period.

### Error: `invalid_client: assertion_lifetime_exceeds_limit`

**Cause:** JWT `exp` is too far in the future (e.g., now+7200 when IS 7.3 max is 600s)
**Fix:** Set `exp` to `now + 300` (5 minutes)

### Error: `invalid_client: assertion_already_used`

**Cause:** Same `jti` used in two requests
**Fix:** Generate a fresh UUIDv4 for each request

### Error: `invalid_client: aud_mismatch`

**Cause:** JWT `aud` doesn't match the token endpoint URL
**Fix:** Ensure `aud` is exactly `https://<is-host>:9443/oauth2/token`
